    <p id="para-00005">Another representation of rational numbers is as a mixed number, such as <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> (<a href="3-4-rational-numbers#fig-00003" class="autogenerated-content" aria-label="View Figure 3.23">Figure 3.23</a>). This represents a whole number (2 in this case), plus a fraction (the <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span>).</p>
    <div class="os-figure" id="fig-00003"><figure class="numbered ui-has-child-figcaption" data-id="fig-00003">
    <span data-type="media" data-alt="Two whole pizzas and 5 slices of a third pizza. The whole pizzas have 8 slices each.">
    <button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of Two whole pizzas and 5 slices of a third pizza. The whole pizzas have 8 slices each." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/9b80ebb47f39b03978239de70a4b2efd76f5f8fc" data-media-type="image/jpg" alt="Two whole pizzas and 5 slices of a third pizza. The whole pizzas have 8 slices each." width="1188" height="381" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/9b80ebb47f39b03978239de70a4b2efd76f5f8fc"></button>
    </span>
    
