<div class="body"><h4 data-type="title">Identifying Rational Numbers</h4>
    <div data-type="exercise" id="exer-00003" class="unnumbered"><header></header><section>
    <div data-type="problem" id="prob-00003"><div class="os-problem-container">
    <p id="para-00018">Determine which of the following are rational numbers:</p>
    <ol id="list-00004" type="1">
    <li><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>73</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><msqrt><mrow><mn>73</mn></mrow></msqrt></annotation-xml></semantics></math></li>
    <li><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>4.556</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>4.556</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math></li>
    <li><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>3</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></annotation-xml></semantics></math></li>
    <li><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>41</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mfrac><mrow><mn>41</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow></mfrac></annotation-xml></semantics></math></li><li><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></li>
    </ol>
    </div></div>
    <details data-type="solution" id="sol-00002" aria-label="Show/Hide Solution">
        <summary class="btn-link ui-toggle" title="Show/Hide Solution" data-content="Show/Hide Solution"></summary>
        <section class="ui-body" role="alert"><h4 data-type="solution-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Solution</span>
</h4>
<div class="os-solution-container">
    <ol id="list-00005" type="1">
    <li>Since 73 is not a perfect square, its square root is not a rational number. This can also be seen when a calculator is used. Entering <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>73</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><msqrt><mrow><mn>73</mn></mrow></msqrt></annotation-xml></semantics></math> into a calculator results in 8.544003745317 (and then more decimal values after that). There is no repeated pattern, so this is not a rational number.</li>
    <li>Since 4.556 is a decimal that terminates, this is a rational number.</li>
    <li><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>3</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></annotation-xml></semantics></math> is a mixed number, so it is a rational number.</li>
    <li><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>41</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mfrac><mrow><mn>41</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow></mfrac></annotation-xml></semantics></math> is an integer divided by an integer, so it is a rational number.</li>
    <li><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mn>5.646464...</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mn>5.646464...</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math> is a decimal that repeats a pattern, so it is a rational number.</li>
    </ol>
