    <section data-depth="1" id="sect-00009"><h3 data-type="title">Applying the Density Property of Rational Numbers</h3>
    <p id="para-00173">Between any two rational numbers, there is another rational number. This is called the <strong>density property</strong> of the rational numbers.</p>
    <p id="para-00174">Finding a rational number between any two rational numbers is very straightforward.</p>
    <p id="para-00175"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Add the two rational numbers.</p>
    <p id="para-00176"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Divide that result by 2.</p>
    <p id="para-00177">The result is always a rational number. This follows what we know about rational numbers. If two fractions are added, then the result is a fraction. Also, when a fraction is divided by a fraction (and 2 is a fraction), then we get another fraction. This two-step process will give a rational number, provided the first two numbers were rational.</p>
    <div data-type="example" id="exam-00021" class="ui-has-child-title"><header><h3 class="os-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Example </span>
  <span class="os-number">3.71</span>
  <span class="os-divider"> </span>
</h3></header><section>
<div class="body"><h4 data-type="title">Applying the Density Property of Rational Numbers</h4>
    <div data-type="exercise" id="exer-00041" class="unnumbered"><header></header><section>
    <div data-type="problem" id="prob-00041"><div class="os-problem-container">
    <p id="para-00178">Demonstrate the density property of rational numbers by finding a rational number between <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfrac></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> and <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfrac></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span>.</p>
    </div></div>
    <details data-type="solution" id="sol-00021" aria-label="Show/Hide Solution">
