</h3></header><section>
<div class="body"><h4 data-type="title">Determining the Number of Specialty Pizzas</h4>
    <div data-type="exercise" id="exer-00045" class="unnumbered"><header></header><section>
    <div data-type="problem" id="prob-00045"><div class="os-problem-container">
    <p id="para-00192">At Bella’s Pizza, one-third of the pizzas that are ordered are one of their specialty varieties. If there are 273 pizzas ordered, how many were specialty pizzas?</p>
    </div></div>
    <details data-type="solution" id="sol-00023" aria-label="Show/Hide Solution">
        <summary class="btn-link ui-toggle" title="Show/Hide Solution" data-content="Show/Hide Solution"></summary>
        <section class="ui-body" role="alert"><h4 data-type="solution-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Solution</span>
</h4>
<div class="os-solution-container">
    <p id="para-00193">One-third of the whole are specialty pizzas, so we need one-third of 273, which gives <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>273</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>273</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>91</mn></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>273</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>273</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>91</mn></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span>, found by dividing 273 by 3. So, 91 of the pizzas that were ordered were specialty pizzas.</p>
    </div>
</section>
      </details>
    </section></div>
