</h3></header><section>
<div class="body"><h4 data-type="title">Converting Centimeters to Inches</h4>
    <div data-type="exercise" id="exer-00049" class="unnumbered"><header></header><section>
    <div data-type="problem" id="prob-00049"><div class="os-problem-container">
    <p id="para-00201">It is known that 1 inch is 2.54 centimeters. Use this to convert 100 centimeters into inches.</p>
    </div></div>
    <details data-type="solution" id="sol-00025" aria-label="Show/Hide Solution">
        <summary class="btn-link ui-toggle" title="Show/Hide Solution" data-content="Show/Hide Solution"></summary>
        <section class="ui-body" role="alert"><h4 data-type="solution-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Solution</span>
</h4>
<div class="os-solution-container">
    <p id="para-00202">We know that 1 inch = 2.54 cm. Since we are converting from centimeters, when we create the fraction we use, make sure the centimeter part of the equivalence is in the denominator, <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>in</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2.54</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>in</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2.54</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span>. To convert the 100 cm to inches, multiply 100 by <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>in</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2.54</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>in</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2.54</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span>. Notice the inch part is in the numerator since we’re converting <em data-effect="italics">to</em> inches, and the centimeter part is in the denominator since we are converting <em data-effect="italics">from</em> centimeters. Performing this and rounding to three decimal places, we obtain <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>in</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2.54</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>39.370</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>in</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mn>100</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>in</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2.54</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>39.370</mn><mspace width="0.28em"></mspace><mtext>in</mtext></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span>. This means 100 cm equals 39.370 in.</p>
    </div>
</section>
      </details>
    </section></div>
