    <section data-depth="1" id="sect-00012"><h3 data-type="title">Defining and Applying Percent</h3>
    <p id="para-00205">A <strong>percent</strong> is a specific rational number and is literally per 100. <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mi>n</mi></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> percent, denoted <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mi>n</mi></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span>%, is the fraction <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span>.</p>
