    <li>The total is 300, and the percentage is 40. Using the decimal form of 40% and multiplying we obtain <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.40</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mn>0.40</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math>.</li>
    <li>The total is 190, and the percentage is 64. Using the decimal form of 64% and multiplying we obtain <math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.64</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>190</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>121.6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mn>0.64</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>190</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>121.6</mn></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math>.</li>
    </ol>
